@format 1
@id processing.run-job
@title Run FFmpeg job
@area 5. Processing and FFmpeg
@entry input
@summary Validate one claimed item, run its FFmpeg stages, and commit success, retry, cancellation, or failure according to the path actually reached.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@allow-cycle true
@related queue.claim-work, processing.source-output-collision, processing.complete, processing.retry, queue.cancel-work
@tag ffmpeg
@tag job

@alias runner = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LRunner
@alias job = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LJob
@alias encode = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LEncode
@alias probe = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LProbe
@alias schedule = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LSchedule
@alias roster = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PRoster

[input] Worker receives claimed work <input>
- Create a job for the claimed item and worker token @ runner.LRunnerLoopRun(...)
- Begin execution of that item @ job.LJobRun(...)
> validate

[validate] Validate stored work <decision>
- Validate required sources, output information, and normalized input/output path separation @ job.LJobValidate(...)
- Compare the final output path with every input before any collision policy can run @ job.LJobInputCollisionCheck(...)
? "Stored work is invalid" > invalid
? "Stored work is valid" > prepare

[invalid] Commit validation failure <error>
- Mark the item failed, commit its message, and reload the schedule @ job.LJobRun(...)
- Remove its attempt record and count a runner failure @ job.LJobRun(...)
> invalid-visible

[invalid-visible] Validation failure is visible <output>
- Display the failed reason first in the selected item's detail pane @ roster.PRosterDetailUpdate(...)
= Invalid stored work never starts FFmpeg and its persisted reason is shown at the top of job details.

[prepare] Prepare execution <process>
- Register the live item and start lease renewal @ job.LJobRun(...)
- Create the output directory and apply collision policy @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
- Build the required FFmpeg stages @ encode.LEncodeStagesBuild(...)
> guarded

[guarded] Enter guarded execution <decision>
- Enter the guarded stage, retry, probe, and commit block @ job.LJobRun(...)
? "Guarded execution continues normally" > stages
? "Cancellation throws OperationCanceledException" > operation-cancelled
? "Another exception escapes a guarded operation" > exception

[stages] Run the next stage <external>
- Attach and start the FFmpeg process @ job.LJobStageRun(...)
- Read progress blocks and publish phase and percentage @ job.LJobProgressRead(...)
- Collect standard error and process exit state @ job.LJobStageRun(...)
> exit

[exit] Evaluate stage result <decision>
? "Another stage remains after success" > stages [loop]
? "All stages succeed" > probe
? "Explicit item cancellation causes nonzero exit" > cancel
? "FFmpeg fails and retry starts" > retry
? "FFmpeg failure is final" > probe

[cancel] Commit explicit cancellation <storage>
- Request durable cancellation for the item @ job.LJobRun(...)
- File the item as cancelled and remove partial output @ schedule.LScheduleItemCancel(...)
> cancelled

[retry] Requeue failed attempt <output>
> map:processing.retry

[probe] Inspect normal process result <process>
- Probe source and output sizes and media properties after normal process completion @ job.LJobRun(...)
- Probe the output keyframe interval when applicable @ probe.LProbeIntervalRead(...)
> commit

[commit] Commit normal completion <storage>
- Commit success when the exit code is zero, otherwise commit final FFmpeg failure @ job.LJobRun(...)
- Reload the schedule and update runner failure state when required @ job.LJobRun(...)
> map:processing.complete

[cancelled] Explicit cancellation complete <output>
= The item is restartable from cancelled storage and the runner continues with the queue.

[operation-cancelled] Runner cancellation observed <output>
- Log cancellation, remove live process/item registrations, stop lease renewal, and clear temporary stages @ job.LJobRun(...) / finally
= This path neither retries nor commits a durable failure or cancellation in LJobRun; runner cancellation and later claim recovery govern the queued record.

[exception] Evaluate execution exception <decision>
- Catch an execution exception that bypasses normal output probing @ job.LJobRun(...)
? "Exception retry starts" > retry
? "Exception failure is final" > exception-failed

[exception-failed] Commit exception failure <error>
- Commit the exception message as final failure without probing output @ job.LJobRun(...)
= The failed item is durable and the runner records a failure.
